<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tatarstan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Republic of Tatarstan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tatarstan is a republic of the Russian Federation on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and lower Kama, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a>. Its territory was the core of Volga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and later of the Khanate of Kazan, conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1552. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatar-assr">Tatar Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic</a> was created in 1920, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> and Russians make up most of its population of about four million.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tatarstan.jpg" alt="Tatarstan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Urmas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Tatarstan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
